Upstream names: githubcopilot, kilocode, kimi, kiro, mistral, and qwen where different.
Amp, Antigravity, DeepSeek, Junie, Kimi, Mistral Vibe, Qoder, and Qwen use the upstream
`-color.svg` variants; their original colors and gradients are preserved.
The Codex color mark uses the monochrome mark's geometry with the original color
gradient, without an app-tile background, so both variants have identical bounds.
Kiro uses the monochrome mark's geometry in its original purple (#9046FF), without
the app-tile background, to preserve the same silhouette in both states.
CodeBuddy likewise omits the app tile and applies its original gradient to the mark.
Kimi's neutral letter uses currentColor for light/dark surfaces; its blue accent is unchanged.
The `-mono.svg` files use Lobe Icons' corresponding monochrome marks, including
Codex, Claude, Gemini, and TRAE. VS Code's monochrome mark derives from its existing
color artwork. These variants use currentColor for a uniform UI tone.

